/**
 * Responsive / horizontal-overflow checker for the customer portal (and any other URL).
 *
 *   npx tsx scripts/check-responsive.ts --base http://localhost:3000 --cookie "$SESSION_JWT"
 *
 * For every route x viewport x theme it opens the page in headless Chromium and reports:
 *   - PAGE OVERFLOW   : document scrollWidth > viewport width (the page itself scrolls sideways)
 *   - WIDE ELEMENTS   : visible elements whose box pokes past the viewport edge and is NOT inside a
 *                       horizontally scrollable container (those are fine) or an aria-hidden /
 *                       pointer-events:none decoration
 *   - SMALL TAPS      : (viewports <= 820px) visible buttons / links / inputs under 40px tall, informational only
 *   - NO VIEWPORT META / console page errors
 * Exits 1 if any PAGE OVERFLOW or WIDE ELEMENTS were found (unless --no-fail).
 *
 * Options
 *   --base URL           default http://localhost:3000
 *   --cookie JWT         session cookie VALUE (or env RESP_COOKIE); omit for public pages
 *   --cookie-name NAME   default nxeon_session (env NXEON_COOKIE_NAME)
 *   --routes a,b,c       override the route list (default: the customer portal list below)
 *   --discover           also visit the first N detail pages linked from list pages (servers/domains/...)
 *   --viewports list     default 360x740,390x844,414x896,768x1024,1024x768,1440x900
 *   --themes list        default dark,light
 *   --out DIR            write screenshots (png) + results.json here (screenshots only with --shots)
 *   --shots              save a full-page screenshot per combination
 *   --tabs               on server detail pages also visit ?tab=<each tab>
 *   --no-fail            always exit 0
 *   --settle MS          extra wait after load (default 1200)
 *
 * Needs `playwright` (already a dev dependency) and a Chromium: `npx playwright install chromium`.
 */
