     for the live portal. Fixed chrome mounted OUTSIDE the shell subtree — the
     terminal dock, MatrixProvider — offsets itself by `--nx-rail-w` and falls
     back to 15rem when nobody sets it. Only the portal shell ever did, so on
     Nexion the dock sat at 240px against a rail that is 76px at lg and 248px
     at xl: a 164px dead gutter down its left, then an 8px overlap. Same shape
     as the providers this shell kept dropping — a thing the portal shell owns
     that was never ported.

     Driven by matchMedia rather than CSS because the value has to land on
     documentElement: the dock is a sibling of the shell root, so it cannot
     inherit a variable declared on it, and the portal shell writes this as an
     inline style, which a stylesheet rule could never outrank. */
  useEffect(() => {
    const lg = window.matchMedia("(min-width: 1024px)");
    const xl = window.matchMedia("(min-width: 1280px)");
